---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Sparkles from '../components/pixel/Sparkles.astro';
---

<Base title="Subha Vadlamannati">
  <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Subha Vadlamannati</h1>
    <Sparkles />
  </div>

  <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-10 sm:flex-row">
    <div class="w-full shrink-0 sm:w-[200px]">
      <img
        src="/images/103_1511 Copy.png"
        alt="Subha Vadlamannati"
        class="w-full max-w-[200px] rounded-lg"
      />

      <div class="mt-5">
        <h3 class="font-pixel text-[11px] lowercase text-ink">contact</h3>
        <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm text-soft">
          <li>subha2@stanford.edu</li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/subha-v" class="quiet-link underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-sakura-bright">Github</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/subhavadlamannati/" class="quiet-link underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-sakura-bright">LinkedIn</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://x.com/subha_v1" class="quiet-link underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-sakura-bright">Twitter</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <img
        src="/images/Gemini_Generated_Image_xdlcs9xdlcs9xdlc-removebg-preview.png"
        alt="Pixel art of Dawn hugging Piplup"
        class="pixel-sprite mt-8 hidden w-28 opacity-90 sm:block"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="prose min-w-0">
      <p>
        Hi! I'm Subha. I'm a student at Stanford studying Computer Science. I'm interested broadly
        in NLP, reinforcement learning, and making GPUs fast(er)! I'm passionate about building
        performant systems that are accessible to all.
      </p>

      <p>
        Currently, I'm working at <a href="https://hazyresearch.stanford.edu/">Hazy Research</a> on
        campus to help with their ThunderKittens work, as well as advancing ethical NLP research at
        my nonprofit, <a href="https://opennlplabs.org/">OpenNLP Labs</a> (join us!). In the past,
        I've worked at <a href="https://saltlab.stanford.edu/">Stanford's SALT</a> lab and
        <a href="https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~neulab/">CMU's Neulab</a> to develop an open-source image
        editing platform for culturally diverse tasks, as well as developing a partial tensorization
        algorithm to compress transformer layers in VLMs. I also organize
        <a href="https://treehacks.com/">TreeHacks</a>, the largest collegiate hackathon in the
        world, as well as help out with Stanford's Machine Learning Lab (MLab) as a TA.
      </p>

      <p>
        In my free time, I love to draw, so feel free to check out some of my art
        <a href="/art">here</a>. I'm also trying to maintain a blog with my course notes and other
        helpful information, so please check it out!
      </p>

      <p>Please feel free to reach out! subha2 [at] stanford [dot] edu.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
